WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.468
United States Supreme Court

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:04.504
dealing Trump a major blow today, siding

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:05.805
with a House committee

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:07.741
seeking his tax returns.

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:10.010
CNN's senior Supreme Court analyst

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:12.045
Joan Biskupic has more information

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:12.545
for us.

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:14.614
So, Joan, what does this ruling mean?

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:15.515
This has been going on

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:17.017
for more than three years, Wolf.

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:18.284
The House Ways and Means

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:20.086
Committee has been trying to obtain

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:21.221
Donald former

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:22.355
President Trump's

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.357
tax returns as part of it.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.926
Look at whether the IRS audits

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:29.462
of presidential records, how it works

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.364
should it be revised?

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:32.966
And the committee had argued

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:35.101
that it has a legitimate legislative

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:36.403
purpose on this.

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:39.072
And Trump had countered it, saying

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:40.340
this is just a witch hunt.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.509
It's just an effort to embarrass him.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.711
He had lost in lower courts

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:46.112
and the former president

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:48.281
had made a last ditch effort to the U.S.

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:49.215
Supreme Court.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:53.386
And today, in a very brief two sentence

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.321
denial said,

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.991
no, we're not going to intervene.

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:00.193
The lower court decision stand.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:00.994
And what this means

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:02.328
now is that the House Ways

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:03.930
and Means Committee

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.732
currently run by Democrats

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.834
currently for a short period.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:08.668
Exactly.

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:11.271
Should be able to obtain from the IRS

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:13.473
the former president's tax returns.

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:15.775
And the committee chairman said today

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:17.043
that they were going to move forward

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:19.312
and try to continue their exploration

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:20.480
of exactly

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.748
what's in his tax returns

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:24.284
and whether the IRS audit

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:26.453
program needs any kind of revision.

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:27.921
And it looked like

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:28.888
it was pretty unanimous.

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:29.456
The Supreme Court.

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:31.191
Well, that's an excellent question

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:33.259
because on paper, on what we got

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:34.794
from the Supreme Court,

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:36.663
there were no recorded dissents.

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:38.098
But, Wolf, my experiences

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:39.732
that sometimes there might be dissents

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:40.533
behind the scenes

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:41.134
and they just don't

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:42.435
want to go public with it.

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.604
But if they didn't go public with it,

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:46.106
all we've got is a flat out

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.740
rejection of the former president,

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.709
even the Supreme Court justices

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:51.511
appointed by Trump. Exactly right.

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:52.912
At least we're silent on this, right?

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:53.813
That's exactly right.

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.582
John, thank you very, very much.

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:57.484
Let's get some more analysis right now.

00:01:57.484 --> 00:01:58.051
Joining us,

00:01:58.051 --> 00:01:58.918
defense attorney

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:00.620
Jan Wu and the state attorney

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:01.821
for Palm Beach County

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:03.423
in Florida, Dave Aronberg.

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:05.492
Paula Reed is still back with us as well.

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:06.359
Shannon,

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:08.428
let me begin with this face off

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:10.063
between the Justice Department

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:12.465
and the former president's legal team.

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:14.667
Based on what we heard today.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:15.268
Do you expect

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:16.469
federal prosecutors

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:17.637
will be successful

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:18.738
in getting rid

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:20.440
of the so-called special master,

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:21.808
reviewing the documents

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.743
recovered from Mar a Lago?

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:24.911
Judging from what

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:25.545
we've heard

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:26.779
and as Paul was referencing

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:28.548
the questions from the panel,

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.517
it seems like that is a possibility.

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:32.185
I mean, I would applaud that decision.

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:34.687
I think it is very dangerous

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.723
for the precedent of letting

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:37.724
criminal defendants

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:40.960
interpose a civil type of mechanism

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:43.196
to basically slow down

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:44.397
the criminal prosecution.

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:46.132
So I think that may happen

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:48.201
given the direction that the courts.

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:49.536
The Court of appeals questions

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:51.137
seem to be going in Wolf.

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:51.804
Well, Paula,

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.506
how significant would a Justice

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:54.407
Department victory

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:56.142
be for the special counsel?

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:58.178
The new special counsel, Jack Smith,

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:02.081
Incredibly significant,

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:03.483
Wolf, because that would allow them

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:05.518
to move forward with this investigation

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:07.220
more more swiftly.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.755
And really, time is of the essence.

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:10.590
You heard the attorney general on Friday

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:11.324
when he announced

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:13.126
the appointment of Jack Smith,

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:14.227
the special counsel.

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:15.161
He was assuring people

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:15.895
that this appointment

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:17.463
would not slow this down.

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:19.165
There are concerns about how long

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:20.333
these investigations

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:21.334
are going to drag out,

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.303
especially given the 2024

00:03:23.303 --> 00:03:25.405
presidential election cycle.

00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:26.606
So if they can remove

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:27.907
this review process,

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:28.875
that would allow them

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:30.176
to move more quickly

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:31.678
Now, I've also talked to someone

00:03:31.678 --> 00:03:32.645
Jack Smith used to work

00:03:32.645 --> 00:03:33.780
for the Justice Department.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:34.214
He said, look,

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:35.415
this is not a guy that Donald

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:36.583
who doesn't sit on things.

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:38.251
He does move swiftly.

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:38.785
And this

00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:40.987
this would really be a win for him.

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:41.721
Dave Aronberg,

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:43.256
let's turn to this decision

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:45.024
from the United States Supreme Court

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:45.992
today to allow

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:47.460
the House of Representatives,

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:48.828
this committee in the House

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:50.663
to review former President Trump's

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:51.831
tax returns.

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:53.099
Trump's legal team

00:03:53.099 --> 00:03:54.767
has continuously fought

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.703
to keep his tax returns secret.

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:58.871
Just how significant of a loss is this

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.106
for the former president?

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:02.508
Wolf, it's a

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:03.543
big loss because

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:04.677
the Trump legal strategy

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:06.546
has always been delay, delay, delay.

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:07.146
I think they knew

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:07.880
they were going to lose,

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.115
but they wanted to

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:10.483
to draw it out long enough

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:11.384
until the Republicans

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:12.785
could get control of Congress

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:14.420
while they're six weeks short.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:15.922
The Democrats are now going to be able

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:18.024
to get these tax returns

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:18.858
and possibly

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:20.760
hand them over to DOJ

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:21.394
if there are

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:22.862
some criminal evidence there.

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:24.330
You know,
the federal law is pretty clear here.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.598
The Ways and Means Committee

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:27.567
has the authority to see any taxpayer's

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:28.434
documents

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:29.168
and Congress

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:30.336
has broad lawmaking

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:31.471
and oversight authority.

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:32.772
So this was always going to go

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:33.573
the government's way.

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:35.008
It was just a question of when.

00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:36.576
And, you know, in the end,

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:37.710
this is only an issue

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.479
because Trump is the first president

00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:39.979
in modern

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:40.780
history, history

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:43.016
to refuse to turn over his taxes

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:43.916
to the American public.

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:44.984
He promised to do so.

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:46.352
He never did so, Wolf.

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:47.854
Somewhere in Tallahassee,

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:50.223
Rhonda Santos is smiling.

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:50.957
Good point.

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:51.791
You know, Shannon,

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:52.825
what information

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:54.761
can this House committee glean

00:04:54.761 --> 00:04:56.996
from these tax documents and what impact

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.531
might this have on the former

00:04:58.531 --> 00:04:59.732
president's various

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:02.402
outstanding legal fights?

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:04.671
I think they can glean a lot from it.

00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:05.672
Less clear

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:07.573
exactly what we as the public

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.442
will get to see from it.

00:05:09.442 --> 00:05:11.911
But I think one issue is that

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:13.413
he's bragged

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:15.448
about the tax avoidance strategies,

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:18.785
and that may be very damning evidence

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:19.352
of his.

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:20.286
What's revealed

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:21.521
corroborates the idea

00:05:21.521 --> 00:05:22.622
that he's exaggerated

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:23.823
his inflated things.

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:26.259
As we're taking a look in New York State

00:05:26.259 --> 00:05:26.893
right now

00:05:26.893 --> 00:05:27.393
at whether

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:28.061
there was tax

00:05:28.061 --> 00:05:30.296
avoidance strategies being used

00:05:30.296 --> 00:05:31.397
by the company.

00:05:31.397 --> 00:05:33.266
So it's very valuable evidence.

00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:33.766
That's why

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:34.500
people generally

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.668
don't like

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:36.669
to have their tax returns

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:37.036
revealed,

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:37.537
because there's

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:38.805
a lot of valuable evidence

00:05:38.805 --> 00:05:40.573
that can be mined from that.

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:42.542
I mean, with Trump, I mean, the

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:44.010
the seeking of his tax

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.611
returns has been like the Holy Grail

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:46.412
in Trumpworld.

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:48.715
I mean, he's fought so hard against it.

00:05:48.748 --> 00:05:50.583
And I think one interesting point

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:51.584
to Dave's point,

00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:52.785
too, is by fighting

00:05:52.785 --> 00:05:55.455
so hard on every single issue,

00:05:55.888 --> 00:05:57.023
it creates the illusion

00:05:57.023 --> 00:05:58.825
sometimes that a setback

00:05:58.825 --> 00:06:00.093
is a great victory.

00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:01.594
This is just Congress

00:06:01.594 --> 00:06:03.096
doing what it's supposed to do.

00:06:03.096 --> 00:06:03.529
And he managed

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:05.465
to drag out for such a long time.

00:06:05.465 --> 00:06:06.599
Where it goes from here

00:06:06.599 --> 00:06:08.501
really does remain to be seen.

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:10.536
We'll find out fairly soon.

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:12.605
Paula, as you know, Republican Senator

00:06:12.605 --> 00:06:13.406
Lindsey Graham

00:06:13.406 --> 00:06:15.341
today completed his appearance

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:16.542
before the Georgia

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:18.611
special grand jury investigating efforts

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:20.546
to overturn the 2020

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:22.014
presidential election.

00:06:22.014 --> 00:06:24.751
How great a threat does this case pose

00:06:24.984 --> 00:06:26.185
to Trump? Himself?

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:29.655
Well, I've asked the

00:06:29.655 --> 00:06:30.923
former president's attorneys

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:32.091
that exact question, Wolf,

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:33.693
and they've told me that they believe

00:06:33.693 --> 00:06:35.661
that the investigation in Fulton County

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:36.129
looking into

00:06:36.129 --> 00:06:36.796
whether the former

00:06:36.796 --> 00:06:38.297
president and his associates

00:06:38.297 --> 00:06:40.233
tried to interfere in the 2020

00:06:40.233 --> 00:06:41.367
presidential election,

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:43.035
that is highly likely

00:06:43.035 --> 00:06:43.503
that he could

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:44.737
potentially be charged there.

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:46.105
They think of all the investigations

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:47.073
that is the one

00:06:47.073 --> 00:06:48.307
that arguably their immediate

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:49.375
in the immediate future

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:50.610
the most concerned about.

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:51.778
Now they would also tell you that

00:06:51.778 --> 00:06:52.378
they don't think

00:06:52.378 --> 00:06:52.745
the case

00:06:52.745 --> 00:06:53.846
will ultimately stick

00:06:53.846 --> 00:06:55.314
and there wouldn't be a conviction

00:06:55.314 --> 00:06:57.150
if charges are actually brought.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:57.917
But the senator is

00:06:57.917 --> 00:06:59.218
just the most recent

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:01.087
in a line of high profile witnesses,

00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:02.722
including the governor of Georgia,

00:07:02.722 --> 00:07:04.323
White House aides who have appeared

00:07:04.323 --> 00:07:05.725
just in the past few weeks.

00:07:05.725 --> 00:07:07.860
So that investigation is active, ongoing

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.562
and even his own attorneys say,

00:07:09.562 --> 00:07:10.696
yes, they're concerned about

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:12.064
what's going on in Fulton County.

00:07:12.064 --> 00:07:13.166
Very significant legal

00:07:13.166 --> 00:07:14.634
developments unfolding today.

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:16.135
Guys, thank you very, very much.

